---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="About Betting Maths"
  description="Learn why Betting Maths exists, what we publish, how our calculations and analysis are checked, and how we approach betting content responsibly."
>
  <section class="content-card">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Betting Maths</p>
    <h1>About Betting Maths</h1>
    <p class="lead">Betting Maths is an independent educational website dedicated to explaining and investigating the mathematics behind betting markets.</p>
    <div class="callout"><strong>Our purpose:</strong> help readers understand what betting numbers actually mean through free calculators, plain-English guides and transparent mathematical analysis. We do not provide betting tips, predictions or guaranteed profit systems.</div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Why Betting Maths exists</h2>
    <p>Betting is full of numbers that can look more intuitive than they really are. Odds contain implied probabilities. A market can contain margin. Exchange bets create liability. Each-way terms alter the return. Accumulator prices multiply. Cash-out offers convert uncertainty into a price.</p>
    <p>Betting Maths exists to make those mechanics visible. Rather than telling a reader what to bet on, the site aims to show the calculation, explain the assumptions and help the reader understand the trade-off.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>What we publish</h2>
    <div class="related-grid">
      <a class="related-card" href="/calculators/"><h3>Calculators</h3><p>Interactive tools for odds, margin, staking, exchange liability, each-way settlement and other betting calculations.</p></a>
      <a class="related-card" href="/guides/"><h3>Guides</h3><p>Plain-English explanations of the concepts and formulas behind the tools.</p></a>
      <a class="related-card" href="/analysis/"><h3>Analysis</h3><p>Original worked investigations that start with a question and use transparent mathematics to examine it.</p></a>
    </div>
    <p>These three layers are intended to work together. A calculator gives a result, a guide explains the concept, and an analysis can explore what happens when the same mathematics is applied to a deeper question.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>How we establish trust</h2>
    <p>Betting Maths does not ask readers to accept a calculation because of a claimed secret system or uncheckable expertise. Our preferred approach is to show enough of the working for a reader to reproduce the result.</p>
    <ul class="standard-list">
      <li>Important formulas are shown on calculator, guide or methodology pages.</li>
      <li>Modelled analysis states its assumptions.</li>
      <li>Observed data will be distinguished from hypothetical examples.</li>
      <li>Probability estimates are labelled as estimates rather than facts.</li>
      <li>Important limitations are included when they affect interpretation.</li>
      <li>External rules or factual claims should use appropriate primary sources where relevant.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button primary" href="/methodology/">Calculation Methodology</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial Standards</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Independence and commercial content</h2>
    <p>Betting Maths is independently produced and maintained. The site may be funded through advertising and may consider appropriate commercial or affiliate relationships in the future.</p>
    <p>Commercial relationships should not change a mathematical result or determine the conclusion of an analysis. Where a relationship is relevant to a page, it should be disclosed clearly.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>What Betting Maths does not do</h2>
    <ul class="standard-list">
      <li>We do not publish betting tips or selections.</li>
      <li>We do not predict sporting outcomes.</li>
      <li>We do not guarantee profit.</li>
      <li>We do not accept bets or operate gambling accounts.</li>
      <li>We do not provide personal financial advice.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Even correct mathematics cannot remove the uncertainty of an event. Real outcomes can also be affected by market rules, settlement rules, odds movement, commission, liquidity, restrictions and human error.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Responsible gambling</h2>
    <p>Understanding odds and probability should make risk clearer, not make gambling look risk-free. Betting Maths maintains dedicated responsible gambling information and links to UK support resources.</p>
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button primary" href="/responsible-gambling/">Responsible Gambling</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-card article-section">
    <h2>Corrections and contact</h2>
    <p>Calculations and explanations should be open to correction. If you spot a reproducible calculation error, broken page or factual issue, the contact page explains the current reporting route.</p>
    <div class="button-row"><a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact and Corrections</a></div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .article-section { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
    .standard-list { padding-left: 1.3rem; }
    .standard-list li { margin: 0.45rem 0; }
    .related-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
    .related-card { display: block; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 14px; background: var(--color-bg); }
    .related-card:hover { border-color: rgba(31, 138, 91, 0.45); transform: translateY(-2px); }
    .related-card p { margin: 0; }
    @media (max-width: 760px) { .related-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  </style>
</MainLayout>
